// The test tree's project, which an editor and vitest's transform both find
// by name; the transform takes its compiler options, legacy decorators
// included, from here. `typecheck:test` checks the same files through
// `../tsconfig.test.json`. Without this file the TS server infers a project
// that loads every `@types` package, and every test shows `TS2403` clashes
// between `@types/mocha` and `@types/jest`.
//
// `include` is declared, not inherited: the transform applies a config only to
// files its own `include` lists, so a test declaring a decorated class would
// fail to load. `../src` is listed because the tests import it, and a
// composite project rejects an import it does not include (TS6307).
{
  "extends": "../tsconfig.test.json",
  "include": ["../src", ".", "../src/**/*.json"]
}
